      "mergeID": "5e8cc6ad0763e56620f551f3",
      "mergedPostDetails": "1. Mathf is designed for floats, some times you might need extra precision so doubles math functions is necessary.\n2. Mathf doesn't implement all Math functions, for example: IEEERemainder (actually very useful %-operator for floating point), Truncate, DivRem (%-operator for integers, also not available \"from the box\"), hyperbolic functions that some times used in blending/animation time curves.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Need System.Math, UnityEngine.Mathf is not enough! Especially remainder operators.",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5dfd3613669bb745a61b2f9f",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 4
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "We also need math functions for integers. Right now a lot of simple stuff like power and modulo are missing for integers.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
